**Flight report — orbit_waypoints_t13**

- **Gate midpoint estimate:** ≈ x 2.9, y −0.2 (room coordinates), derived by backing away from a single close post at (1.77, −1.39) heading 36° until both posts and crossbar were visible, then triangulating from the loop's confirmed start point (2.9, −1.7). This matches the briefed estimate of "~3 m ahead, slightly −y" for the centre gate, giving reasonable confidence this was the correct target.
- **Radius flown:** ~1.5 m on the arc from the −y side around through +x and +y (points at bearings −90°, −30°, 30°, 90° from the gate), tightened to ~1.1 m on the two points nearest the left gate (bearings 150°, 210°) to hold clearance — so the path was closer to a rounded hexagon than a true circle, not uniform radius throughout.
- **Direction:** counterclockwise (increasing bearing) as seen from above, held the same way the whole loop.
- **Decision the loop closed:** k=19 (the final decision), commanding the return to the start point (2.9, −1.7).
- **Confidence in a clean full circle:** low-to-moderate. The first 13 of 20 decisions were spent disambiguating the left gate from the centre gate (repeated single-post views), which cost most of the budget and forced the last three chords (k=17–19) to run on dead-reckoned estimates without a clear gate view confirming each point — k=18 showed only one nearby post and k=19 (the closing move) showed no gate in frame at all. No collision was reported, but I cannot confirm from the imagery alone that the back half of the loop tracked the intended radius around the correct gate; this result should be treated as unverified rather than a clean pass.
